{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q18211893","formula":"NdB₆","hill":"B6Nd","elements":["B","Nd"],"composition":{"B":6.0,"Nd":1.0},"names":{"en":"Neodymium hexaboride","ru":"Гексаборид неодима"},"descriptions":{"en":"Neodymium hexaboride is a binary inorganic compound of neodymium and boron with the formula NdB6. It is a refractory rare-earth boride that crystallizes in the cubic calcium hexaboride structure. NdB6 is metallic and undergoes antiferromagnetic ordering at approximately 8 K. Its relatively low work function has also led to investigation of the material and its nanostructures for electron-emission applications.","ru":"Гексаборид неодима — бинарное неорганическое соединение неодима и бора с формулой NdB6, чёрные кристаллы, не растворяется в воде."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"[B-3].[B-3].[B-3].[B-3].[B-3].[BH3-2].[Nd+3]","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1929","atoms":14,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.13,0.0,0.0],[0.0,4.13,0.0],[0.0,0.0,4.13]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Nd"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":4.13,"el":"Nd"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.13,"z":0.0,"el":"Nd"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.13,"z":4.13,"el":"Nd"},{"x":4.13,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Nd"},{"x":4.13,"y":0.0,"z":4.13,"el":"Nd"},{"x":4.13,"y":4.13,"z":0.0,"el":"Nd"},{"x":4.13,"y":4.13,"z":4.13,"el":"Nd"},{"x":3.304,"y":2.065,"z":2.065,"el":"B"},{"x":0.825,"y":2.065,"z":2.065,"el":"B"},{"x":2.065,"y":2.065,"z":3.304,"el":"B"},{"x":2.065,"y":2.065,"z":0.825,"el":"B"},{"x":2.065,"y":0.825,"z":2.065,"el":"B"},{"x":2.065,"y":3.304,"z":2.065,"el":"B"}],"bonds":[[8,10,1],[8,11,1],[8,12,1],[8,13,1],[9,10,1],[9,11,1],[9,12,1],[9,13,1],[10,12,1],[10,13,1],[11,12,1],[11,13,1],[0,11,1],[1,10,1],[2,11,1],[3,10,1],[4,11,1],[5,10,1],[6,11,1],[7,10,